# Secrets

- Never read, quote, print, or paste contents of `.env`, `.env.*`, `api/.env`, `api/.env.shared`, `deploy/vps/.env`, `LOCAL-LOGIN.txt`, `VPS-LOGIN.txt`, private keys, or password files.
- Never write secrets into notes, commits, PRs, chat replies, screenshots captions, or logs.
- If a secret is needed for work, refer to the **variable name** only (e.g. `JWT_SECRET`, `GEMINI_API_KEY`) and tell the user to set it in their local/VPS env file.
- If a secret was already shown in chat or a file, warn the user to **rotate** it; do not repeat the value.
- Prefer `*.example` env templates (placeholders only). Real values stay gitignored.
- When debugging auth/mail/AI, log success/failure messages only — never tokens, passwords, connection strings, or API keys.
